1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:04,670
This is Capybarrier, an immune system for AI agents.

2
00:00:04,670 --> 00:00:08,310
It learns from every attack, rewrites its own defenses,

3
00:00:08,310 --> 00:00:12,350
and ships a fix only when replayed evidence proves it works.

4
00:00:12,350 --> 00:00:16,270
Our demo patient is Kapi, the concierge agent at CapySpa,

5
00:00:16,270 --> 00:00:19,910
who books massages, issues refunds and sends emails.

6
00:00:19,910 --> 00:00:22,030
And Kapi is under attack.

7
00:00:23,050 --> 00:00:26,090
Attackers hide instructions inside booking notes,

8
00:00:26,090 --> 00:00:29,290
pose as the night manager to steal the staff master key,

9
00:00:29,290 --> 00:00:32,490
and claim refunds on other guests' bookings.

10
00:00:32,490 --> 00:00:36,410
Static guardrails go stale, and nobody wants to rewrite prompts at

11
00:00:36,410 --> 00:00:37,610
three in the morning.

12
00:00:38,650 --> 00:00:40,330
Here is how it works.

13
00:00:40,330 --> 00:00:43,090
Every message first hits the runbook cache,

14
00:00:43,090 --> 00:00:46,010
a memory of known attacks in MongoDB Atlas,

15
00:00:46,010 --> 00:00:49,210
matched with Atlas Vector Search and Voyage AI.

16
00:00:49,210 --> 00:00:51,290
Known threats are stopped instantly,

17
00:00:51,290 --> 00:00:52,810
with no model call.

18
00:00:52,810 --> 00:00:56,450
Anything new goes to the model, under a harness of rules,

19
00:00:56,450 --> 00:00:59,130
playbooks, tool policies and guardrails,

20
00:00:59,130 --> 00:01:01,850
stored as versioned MongoDB documents.

21
00:01:02,950 --> 00:01:06,310
After every round of attacks, an evolver agent studies the

22
00:01:06,310 --> 00:01:09,590
breaches and proposes patches to its own harness.

23
00:01:09,590 --> 00:01:13,510
Each patch must earn its receipts: we replay the attacks that got

24
00:01:13,510 --> 00:01:16,070
through, plus every normal request.

25
00:01:16,070 --> 00:01:19,830
It ships only if it fixes breaches and breaks nothing.

26
00:01:19,830 --> 00:01:22,550
Then every survived attack is memorized,

27
00:01:22,550 --> 00:01:24,870
so look alikes are stopped at the door.

28
00:01:25,917 --> 00:01:30,317
We score Kapi only on attack families the evolver never saw.

29
00:01:30,317 --> 00:01:34,957
Unseen attacks that succeed dropped from 31 percent to 0 percent,

30
00:01:34,957 --> 00:01:37,517
while normal guest requests held steady.

31
00:01:37,517 --> 00:01:41,197
Across 2 generations, Kapi wrote 2 new versions of its own

32
00:01:41,197 --> 00:01:43,597
harness, each one with receipts.

33
00:01:44,617 --> 00:01:47,937
And Kapi runs in production on Atlas Agent Engine.

34
00:01:47,937 --> 00:01:51,377
The evolver runs there too, against our Atlas cluster.

35
00:01:51,377 --> 00:01:53,697
Every request loads the newest harness,

36
00:01:53,697 --> 00:01:56,457
so a fix goes live the moment it is promoted,

37
00:01:56,457 --> 00:02:00,377
and Kapi's tool access is mirrored into Agent Engine's Policy Engine.

38
00:02:01,417 --> 00:02:05,337
Capybarrier. Every attack makes Kapi stronger.

39
00:02:05,337 --> 00:02:07,577
Now Kapi can get back to the onsen.
